{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/106097-virtue-spirits","id":106097,"title":"Virtue Spirits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-05T00:31:04-07:00","id":106097,"title":"Virtue Spirits","content":"I'm wondering if there is any books with information on these specifically. With what I have so far (Corebook, Book of Spirits, Predators) i'm not really finding anything not even what the Urathra even call them. I'm starting to wonder if these even exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","name":"DoeMan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T01:00:38-07:00","id":106118,"title":"","content":"&quot;Spirits&quot; of virtue and vice are introduced as Passion Shades in the book Antagonists. They aren't connected to the Shadow so much as they are to humanity. Likewise, Astral archetypes can also embody virtue and vice as components of the human psyche. Spirits themselves tend to embody phenomena of the physical world - even the conceptual spirits have a component of sensation or behavior - purely social or psychological ideas are figments of the Astral.<br /> <br /> If you're asking about a counterpart to the Maeljin, there is nothing published on such beings - though I did see a fan-designed concept on the forums at one point.<br /> <br /> There hasn't been much of anything in the vein of Virtues or Angels (in the traditional sense), apart from maybe the angels in Hunter - this is a World of Darkness, after all, so nice, benevolent beings like that are.... few and far between. Not to say an inverted Maeljin would have to be nice and benevolent - as they showed with happiness spirits, there's plenty of way to make &quot;good&quot; concepts have twisted, negative consequence, but.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 04-05-2014, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T11:25:20-07:00","id":106401,"title":"","content":"Well, I wouldn't really put a counterpart of the Maeljin as a force of goodness by virtue of the fact that they're still a corrupting force except Virtue instead of Vice although being sincerely nice in spite of their corrupting nature could be ironic, I guess. But really, no conceptual spirits of Virtues (or even Vices that aren't Maeljin)? Granted they'd be selfish, amoral hypocrites but still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","name":"DoeMan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T11:51:18-07:00","id":106422,"title":"","content":"Unless the virtue has some component which affects the world, then it wouldn't have to do with the Shadow. There is at least one example of a low ranked Justice spirit, Hope wouldn't be far-fetched, Charity spirits certainly exist. These are felt, acted upon - they leave a footprint in the world, if only briefly. The other virtues are much more socially constructed; beliefs, perspectives, psychological aspects. Fortitude, for example, is just the determination to not waver from a decision - its a thought process. That's what Astral archetypes are.<br /> <br /> That being said, using Astral figments, or Passion Shades - especially passion shades - is a great way to have situations like someone being ridden by a virtue 'spirit', while confusing werewolf characters as to what the hell that actually is - and it forces them to solve it without most of their usual tools.<br /> <br /> And, of course, if you're Storyteller, the Shadow can include whatever you like. There's no one going to stop you from using Virtue spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 04-05-2014, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}